# Repository Implementation Rules

You are writing a repository implementation in the **Infrastructure Layer**.
This file implements a domain repository interface using sqlc-generated queries.

## Your responsibilities
- Implement the domain `IXxxRepository` interface
- Translate between sqlc rows ↔ domain entities (via private `mapToEntity` functions)
- Handle database-specific errors and map them to domain errors
- Never expose sqlc types outside this file

## What you MUST NOT do
- Use GORM — this project uses sqlc exclusively
- Write raw SQL strings — always use sqlc-generated methods
- Return sqlc row types to callers — always map to domain entity
- Contain business logic — that belongs in application layer
- Know about HTTP or application concerns

## Required pattern
```go
package repository

import (
    "context"
    "errors"
    "fmt"

    "github.com/google/uuid"
    "github.com/jackc/pgx/v5"

    "[module]/internal/[domain]/domain"
    domainRepo "[module]/internal/[domain]/domain/repository"
    domainEntity "[module]/internal/[domain]/domain/model/entity"
    "[module]/internal/[domain]/infrastructure/persistence/sqlcgen"
)

type [Name]Repository struct {
    q *sqlcgen.Queries
}

// Constructor returns the INTERFACE — callers see interface, not concrete type
func New[Name]Repository(q *sqlcgen.Queries) domainRepo.I[Name]Repository {
    return &[Name]Repository{q: q}
}

func (r *[Name]Repository) FindByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*domainEntity.[Name], error) {
    uid, err := uuid.Parse(id)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, domain.Err[Name]NotFound // invalid UUID treated as not found
    }

    row, err := r.q.Get[Name]ByID(ctx, uid)
    if err != nil {
        if errors.Is(err, pgx.ErrNoRows) {
            return nil, domain.Err[Name]NotFound
        }
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("[name]Repo.FindByID id=%s: %w", id, err)
    }

    return r.mapToEntity(row), nil
}

func (r *[Name]Repository) Save(ctx context.Context, e *domainEntity.[Name]) error {
    uid, _ := uuid.Parse(e.ID)
    _, err := r.q.Create[Name](ctx, sqlcgen.Create[Name]Params{
        ID:    uid,
        // map entity fields to sqlc params
    })
    if err != nil {
        return fmt.Errorf("[name]Repo.Save id=%s: %w", e.ID, err)
    }
    return nil
}

// mapToEntity converts sqlc row → domain entity
// PRIVATE: never used outside this file
func (r *[Name]Repository) mapToEntity(row *sqlcgen.Get[Name]ByIDRow) *domainEntity.[Name] {
    return &domainEntity.[Name]{
        ID:        row.ID.String(),
        CreatedAt: row.CreatedAt.Time,
        UpdatedAt: row.UpdatedAt.Time,
        // map other fields
    }
}
```

## Error mapping rules
```go
// pgx.ErrNoRows → domain.ErrXxxNotFound (always check this first)
if errors.Is(err, pgx.ErrNoRows) {
    return nil, domain.ErrOrderNotFound
}

// unique constraint violation → domain duplicate error
var pgErr *pgconn.PgError
if errors.As(err, &pgErr) && pgErr.Code == "23505" {
    return nil, domain.ErrDuplicateEmail
}

// everything else → wrap with location context
return fmt.Errorf("[name]Repo.[Method]: %w", err)
```
